From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 21:25:47 +0200
Subject: leds: lgm-sso: set the GPTC clock rate before deriving the blink
 table

sso_init_freq() fills priv->freq[] from priv->fpid_clkrate and
priv->gptc_clkrate, but probe assigns priv->gptc_clkrate only after
calling it. The five GPTC-derived ranks are therefore computed against
zero, and stay zero for the life of the device.

priv->freq[] is what maps a requested blink rate onto a hardware rank:
sso_get_blink_rate_idx() returns the first entry that is at least the
requested rate, and a zero entry can never satisfy that. Any rate that
should land on the GPTC or GPTC high-speed source falls through to the
-1 return instead, both callers clamp that to the last rank -- whose
frequency is one of the zeroes -- and delay_to_freq_idx() goes on to
compute 1000 / priv->freq[freq_idx].

Move the assignment ahead of the call.

Fixes: c3987cd2bca3 ("leds: lgm: Add LED controller driver for LGM SoC")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
index 25725a4a330f..f66b7366a816 100644
--- a/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
+++ b/drivers/leds/blink/leds-lgm-sso.c
@@ -879,9 +879,8 @@ static int intel_sso_led_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	INIT_LIST_HEAD(&priv->led_list);
 
 	platform_set_drvdata(pdev, priv);
-	sso_init_freq(priv);
-
 	priv->gptc_clkrate = DEF_GPTC_CLK_RATE;
+	sso_init_freq(priv);
 
 	ret = sso_led_dt_parse(priv);
 	if (ret)
